<title>USA: New US Republican tax plan is net $89 bln cut-aide.</title>
<headline>New US Republican tax plan is net $89 bln cut-aide.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A House-Senate Republican compromise tax plan would cut taxes by a net $89 billion over five years, a congressional aide said Wednesday.</p>
<p>House and Senate Republicans have agreed on a unified tax proposal they will take to negotiations with White House officials.</p>
<p>The tax legislation aims to implement the May budget agreement between congressional leaders and the White House that called for an $85 billion net cut over five years.</p>
</text>
